[?25l> Key design decisions:
- atof in C parses as double then truncates to float — so I parse as f64 then cast to f32
- Q_rsqrt uses memcpy for type-punning — I use to_bits()/from_bits() for identical behavior
- printf("%f", ...) defaults to 6 decimal places — Rust's {:.6} matches this
- The C error message uses argv[0] — I use args[0]
- The C checks argc != 4 (program name + 3 args) — same logic
